  "question": {
    "text": "At what distance (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>) from a convex mirror of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>2.5</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> should a boy stand so that his image has a height equal to half of his height? The principal axis of the mirror is perpendicular to the height of the boy.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>m</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#160;m</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#160;m</mtext></math><br /><br />Thus, he should stand at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>2.5</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the mirror.",
